    summary_en: "On August 3rd, United Fiber Communications received notification of a ransomware attack on its information systems. The company immediately activated internal cybersecurity checks and incident response measures, and has reported the incident to the police. According to preliminary assessments, the event is not expected to impact the company's daily operations. The company has strengthened its network security defenses and continues to intensively monitor the operational status of all systems to ensure the stability and security of its information systems. This incident is a typical ransomware attack, highlighting the continuous threats faced by enterprise information systems. It is recommended that companies establish comprehensive Incident Response Plans (IRP) and regularly conduct system backup and recovery drills to cope with similar cyber attacks.",
