    summary: "近期美國 T-Mobile 曾發生大規模服務中斷，影響了數十萬名用戶，導致許多 iPhone 用戶在數小時內無法使用行動通訊服務，包括無法撥打電話、傳送簡訊或使用行動數據。服務中斷持續約七小時，直到電信業者才宣布服務完全恢復。儘管 T-Mobile 已發出道歉聲明，但並未主動為受影響用戶提供補償。根據用戶回報，受影響的客戶必須主動聯繫 T-Mobile 的客服團隊（例如透過 T-Life 應用程式）才能申請帳單抵扣。用戶報告的補償金額範圍從 $10 到 $80 不等，該筆信用額將適用於未來六個月的帳單。此事件凸顯了電信服務中斷的實務影響，並提醒用戶在服務受損後，需主動掌握權益，聯繫電信業者尋求補償。",
    tags: ["T-Mobile", "iPhone", "服務中斷", "帳單補償", "行動通訊"],
    title_en: "T-Mobile Service Outage: Users Must Proactively Contact for Billing Compensation",
    summary_en: "Recently, T-Mobile in the US experienced a large-scale service outage, affecting hundreds of thousands of users. This resulted in many iPhone users being unable to use mobile communication services for several hours, including making calls, sending texts, or using mobile data. The service disruption lasted approximately seven hours until the carrier announced full service restoration. Although T-Mobile issued an apology statement, they did not proactively offer compensation to affected users. According to user reports, affected customers had to proactively contact T-Mobile's customer service team (for example, via the T-Life app) to apply for a bill credit. Reported compensation amounts ranged from $10 to $80, with the credit applicable to the next six months' bills. This incident highlights the practical impact of telecommunications service disruptions and reminds users that they must proactively assert their rights and contact the carrier to seek compensation after service damage.",
