    title_en: "Apple Files Motion for Preliminary Injunction Against OpenAI, Seeking to Block Use of Stolen Trade Secrets",
    summary_en: "Apple filed a motion with the court seeking a preliminary injunction in its trade secret lawsuit against OpenAI. Apple argues that without an injunction, its trade secrets will suffer 'irreparable harm.' Apple is requesting the court to immediately prevent OpenAI from using or accessing any of Apple's trade secrets, and is also requesting forensic examination of OpenAI's devices, cloud storage, email, Slack, and Teams to recover all confidential information. Although the parties have reached an agreement on three points—ceasing use, ceasing disclosure, and preserving evidence—they failed to reach an agreement on 'allowing forensic examination' and 'searching for confidential information within OpenAI's systems.' Apple emphasized that the longer the time passes, the harder it will be for OpenAI to eliminate its reliance on the stolen information, causing deeper damage. The hearing for this lawsuit is scheduled for October 1, 2026.",
