    category: "重點關注",
    title: "中國修改晶片法律定義：將「半導體積體電路」擴展至包含光學與量子元件的「積體電路」",
    summary: "中國國家知識產權局發布專家意見，修改了晶片相關的智慧財產權法規。此次修法將原先定義的「半導體積體電路」（semiconductor integrated circuit）替換為更廣泛的「積體電路」（integrated circuit）。此舉的目的是為了將光子學（photonic）和量子晶片等新型元件納入法律保護範圍。雖然表面上看，國際上許多晶片仍需半導體作為基板，但修法在法律層面具有重大意義，顯示中國在知識產權保護上不再保守。新規定旨在強化國內的版圖保護法，特別是為了保護包含光學或量子元件的晶片設計，幫助國內晶片製造商（如華為、阿里巴巴等）在版權和設計起源方面獲得更強的法律支持，以應對國內外抄襲。",
    tags: ["中國", "積體電路", "半導體", "光子學", "量子晶片", "智慧財產權"],
    title_en: "China revises chip law definition: Expanding 'semiconductor integrated circuit' to include 'integrated circuit' encompassing optical and quantum components",
    summary_en: "The China National Intellectual Property Administration (CNIPA) has issued expert opinions revising intellectual property laws related to chips. This revision replaces the previously defined 'semiconductor integrated circuit' with the broader term 'integrated circuit.' The purpose of this measure is to include new components such as photonic and quantum chips within the scope of legal protection. Although many chips globally still require semiconductors as a substrate, the legal revision holds significant meaning, indicating that China's approach to intellectual property protection is no longer conservative. The new regulations aim to strengthen domestic map protection laws, especially to protect chip designs that include optical or quantum components, thereby providing stronger legal support for domestic chip manufacturers (such as Huawei and Alibaba) regarding copyright and design origin, in response to both domestic and international infringement.",
    tags_en: ["China", "integrated circuit", "semiconductor", "photonics", "quantum chip", "intellectual property"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Register", url: "https://theregister.com/legal/2026/08/04/china-claims-global-chip-leadership-thanks-to-new-legal-definition-of-integrated-circuits/5282563", lang: "EN" }
    ]
