    summary_en: "Google is actively promoting its co-branded laptop series, 'Googlebook.' Beyond the previously revealed Lenovo version, the latest leaked information showcases the Asus CX9406 model. The device's system is described as 'Aluminum OS' and is positioned as a flagship product for advanced digital professionals, rather than a traditional Chromebook. Aesthetically, the model utilizes 'Ultra-Ceramic Light Alloy,' emphasizing both lightness and durability, claiming to be '34% lighter and 13% more durable.' In terms of hardware configuration, it is expected to feature diverse ports such as USB-C, HDMI, and USB-A, and includes a unique 'Glowbar' indicator light. Although the article provides some specification descriptions, it lacks core technical details such as CPU or storage capacity. This suggests that the Googlebook series product line is rapidly approaching market release, with multiple manufacturers (including Asus and Lenovo) participating in the collaboration, and is expected to deliver a brand-new operating system experience powered by Gemini.",
