    title: "前美國共和黨籍前領導人警告：FCC 無法單方面廢除電視所有權限制法規",
    summary: "本文報導了前美國眾議院多數派領袖 Tom DeLay 的觀點，他警告美國聯邦通信委員會（FCC）沒有法律權力單方面廢除國家電視所有權限制（National Television Ownership Rule）。DeLay 指出，該限制規定單一廣播站所有者不得超過美國所有電視用戶的 39%，此限制已寫入美國法律，因此只有國會（Congress）而非 FCC 可以修改。儘管 FCC 主席 Brendan Carr 已宣布計劃取消此限制，並定於本週投票，DeLay 強調，如果 FCC 想要提高法定上限，必須要求國會通過法律賦予權力。文章回顧了該限制的歷史，指出 FCC 曾於 1985 年實施 25% 的限制，並在 1996 年《電信法案》中被國會提升至 35%，最終定為 39%。",
    tags: ["FCC", "美國法律", "電視所有權限制", "Tom DeLay", "國會權力", "監管法規"],
    title_en: "Former US Republican Leader Warns: FCC Cannot Unilaterally Repeal National Television Ownership Restriction",
    summary_en: "This article reports on the views of former US House Majority Leader Tom DeLay, who warned that the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) does not have the legal authority to unilaterally repeal the National Television Ownership Rule. DeLay pointed out that this restriction stipulates that a single broadcast station owner cannot exceed 39% of all US television users. Since this limit is enshrined in US law, only Congress, not the FCC, can modify it. Although FCC Chairman Brendan Carr has announced plans to repeal this restriction and scheduled a vote this week, DeLay emphasized that if the FCC wishes to raise the statutory limit, it must request Congress to pass legislation granting the authority. The article reviews the history of this restriction, noting that the FCC initially implemented a 25% limit in 1985, which was later raised by Congress to 35% under the Telecommunications Act of 1996, and finally set at 39%.",
    tags_en: ["FCC", "US Law", "Television Ownership Restriction", "Tom DeLay", "Congressional Authority", "Regulatory Rules"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Ars Technica", url: "https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/08/can-trump-fcc-repeal-39-tv-ownership-cap-republican-who-wrote-cap-into-law-says-no", lang: "EN" }
    ]
