    category: "重點關注",
    title: "Linux Foundation成立Tokenomics Foundation，旨在建立AI價值經濟與投資回報率標準",
    summary: "Linux Foundation宣布成立Tokenomics Foundation，這是其持續推動AI相關生態系統的最新舉措。該基金會旨在為AI價值建立開放、中立的產業標準、基準和最佳實踐，特別關注如何衡量AI的投資回報率（ROI）和總體擁有成本（TCO）。該基金會由包括Accenture、IBM、Oracle、SAP、ServiceNow等30家創始成員支持。其路線圖規劃包括定義AI的代幣經濟學（tokenomics）和價值指標，建立AI價值框架來衡量業務影響，並制定衡量AI全成本和服務成本的廠商中立模型。這項舉動顯示Linux Foundation正積極將其生態系擴展至AI的經濟層面，為產業提供統一的價值衡量語言。",
    tags: ["Linux Foundation", "Tokenomics Foundation", "AI", "ROI", "總體擁有成本", "產業標準"],
    title_en: "Linux Foundation Establishes Tokenomics Foundation to Build AI Value Economy and ROI Standards",
    summary_en: "The Linux Foundation has announced the establishment of the Tokenomics Foundation, the latest initiative in its ongoing effort to advance the AI-related ecosystem. The foundation aims to establish open, neutral industry standards, benchmarks, and best practices for AI value, with a particular focus on measuring the Return on Investment (ROI) and Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) of AI. The foundation is supported by 30 founding members, including Accenture, IBM, Oracle, SAP, and ServiceNow. Its roadmap includes defining the tokenomics and value metrics for AI, establishing an AI value framework to measure business impact, and developing a vendor-neutral model to measure the full cost and service cost of AI. This move demonstrates the Linux Foundation's proactive effort to expand its ecosystem into the economic layer of AI, providing a unified language for value measurement across the industry.",
